Happy people are more productive, creative, and cooperative — a 2012 Gallup study found highly engaged (satisfied) workers are 21% more productive than disengaged ones.
National wellbeing metrics (the Nordic countries' HDI scores, Bhutan's Gross National Happiness index) correlate positively with innovation, social cohesion, and economic productivity.
Positive emotions 'broaden and build' (Barbara Fredrickson) — they expand the range of thoughts and actions people consider, leading to more creative problem-solving and better long-term outcomes.
